    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that participant experience is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_17e6c5b28dadba8c\",\"quote\":\"I heard it from the internet and the radio, yes I heard from there\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_af4b95b44869cdce\",\"quote\":\"I heard that it was fatal\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f07140f1b614d322\",\"quote\":\"When I first heard about corona it was a big shock to us and secondly It led to loss of many jobs\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_db954491fdefedce\",\"quote\":\"It is a respiratory disease\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The evidence presents diverse reactions to COVID-19, including fatal reports, job losses, and a disease definition, without establishing institutional procedures as the primary driver of participant experience.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies participant experience, ignoring other potential influences highlighted in the sources.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The sources indicate varied responses, suggesting multiple drivers of experience, not solely institutional factors.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim makes a broad assertion unsupported by the provided evidence, which details individual perceptions and consequences related to COVID-19, rather than a primary driver of participant experience.\"}",
